16	// Conventions
17	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
18	//
19	// A row is a set of cells indexed by integer. Index increases to the RIGHT, so
20	// the left neighbour of cell i is cell i-1 and the right neighbour is cell i+1.
21	//
22	// In the BigInt representation, bit i of the BigInt is cell i. In the naive
23	// representation, array slot i is cell i. The two use the same indexing on
24	// purpose, so a row from one can be compared to a row from the other slot by
25	// slot with no coordinate translation.
